OpenSearch UI requires explicit permission in the VPC endpoint policy to allow users to access the
application from the VPC. If you no longer want users to access OpenSearch UI from the VPC, you
can remove the permission in the endpoint policy. After this, users encounter a 403 forbidden
error message when attempting to access OpenSearch UI.
For information about updating a VPC endpoint policy, see Update a VPC endpoint policy in the
AWS PrivateLink Guide.
The following is an example of VPC endpoint policy that denies access to the UI applications from
the VPC:
{
"Statement": [{
"Action": ["opensearch:*"],
"Effect": "Allow",
"Principal": "*",
"Resource": "*",
"Condition": {
"StringEquals": {
"opensearch:ApplicationId": [""]
}
}
